// A declaration with NO BODY accepts `@compileFor(FLAG)` and nothing else. `@noheap` gates allocation
// IN a body and `@interrupt`/`@section` attach to EMITTED CODE, so neither has anything to apply to on
// an `extern "<h>";`, an `extern fn` or a `fnptr`. Before this, a stray attribute here was accepted in
// silence — there is no emitter path for a bodyless form, so nothing ever looked at its attributes.
@noheap extern "stdio.h";
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
